From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 06:50:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d3d12: Count a present skipped while minimised as a frame.

DXMT_STATS reports per frame and every 5 s of frames, counted at each
present; a game presenting to a minimised window skipped that count, so
its figures stopped (and no 5 s report came) until it was restored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/d3d12/d3d12_swapchain.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/d3d12/d3d12_swapchain.cpp b/src/d3d12/d3d12_swapchain.cpp
index 9fd2748..6337f8d 100644
--- a/src/d3d12/d3d12_swapchain.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d12/d3d12_swapchain.cpp
@@ -765,6 +765,7 @@ public:
       DXMT_STAT_COUNT("#presents skipped (window minimised)", 1);
       ReleaseSemaphore(present_semaphore_, 1, nullptr);
       presentation_count_ += 1;
+      StatsFrame();  // still a frame: DXMT_STATS's per-frame figures and its 5 s reports go on
       Sleep(16);
       return hr;
     }
